  "notes": "Sheet 0 (MAPA Architects, near Pueblo Edén, Maldonado; a prefabricated cabin of two 12.5 m modules built in a factory outside Montevideo and set among olives in the hills): a long black steel box wrapped in vertical timber slat shutters that glows at dusk, cantilevered out from a dry fieldstone plinth wall that holds the slope (photographs 1 to 3), its end walls of corrugated pale steel with a small panel window, a floor-to-ceiling glass wall opening to the view with a timber lining and floors inside (the last photograph); grass hillside, outcrops of stone, olive and native trees. Modelled: the plinth and its returns, the two-module box with its steel frame, slatted shutters and glazing, the metal end, rocks, trees. Guessed: the exact width (read as about 4.8 m), the plinth's height, tree positions. A private cabin placed at its department only (Maldonado)."
